        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: VAQ-138, VAQ-137, United States Navy\n- Products: Boeing EA-18G Growler, F/A-18F Super Hornet\n- Places: Naval Air Station Whidbey Island, Washington\n- Concepts: electronic attack squadron, electronic warfare aircraft\n\nFacts:\n- VAQ-138, also known as the Yellow Jackets, is a United States Navy expeditionary electronic attack squadron based at Naval Air Station Whidbey Island in Washington.\n- The Boeing EA-18G Growler is an American carrier-based electronic warfare aircraft derived as a specialized version of the two-seat F/A-18F Super Hornet.\n- VAQ-137, also known as the Rooks, is a United States Navy electronic attack squadron based at Naval Air Station Whidbey Island in Washington and flies the Boeing EA-18G Growler.",
